-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Jetpac
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1983
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Jet Pac (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)(16K)[a2][a2].z80
  MD5         5875d535442974a0de82737652854f1f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jetman, the aliens, the rocket parts and the fuel in fuller
              multicolour. Source: enhanced colours from an older Spec256
              conversion (Spectrum Magic's jetpac_.zip), painter not
              established.

  Changes     1.1: writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's ROM plus the
              hooks), so the ROM's own interrupt code can never run the hooks.

  Note        Coloured build (not Dean's Jetpac build). Known issues: none
              found in testing. Missing: pace not measured against the
              original; two-player games not checked; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives

