-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-03

  Replay      free run of 6000 frames IDENTICAL, no recording (20,433 draws,
              100 erases, 23,192 colour paints, 5 clears, 2,193,166 sprite
              pixels); alt ROM image modelled as the Next fills it, from
              NextZXOS's ROM3 then the build's writes: whole image Sinclair's
              48K ROM plus hooks, 0 bytes outside the hooks differ; IM 1
              handler compared with the original's at all 5,149 interrupts,
              IDENTICAL; unit tests 6,816 graphic cases, negative control
              40/40; new negative: the previous partial image (hooks only over
              ROM3) detected at 5,149 of 5,149 interrupts (hook code ran from
              the IM 1 handler) and by 5,367 image bytes

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, whole alt ROM build (2026-11-04):
              loading screen, menu, play and game over back to the menu,
              default and Enhanced, frames viewed; alt ROM image dumped in
              JNext equals the modelled Sinclair-plus-hooks image; with
              NextZXOS's DivMMC 0x0038 trap removed, IM 1 ran Sinclair's
              handler 1,609 times and no ROM3 handler; earlier: the owner
              played the painted build through take-off, rocket and fuel
              appearing; real loader runs were of the previous build

  Coverage    two players not exercised; whole alt ROM image from 2026-11-04:
              the previous build differs only in the alt ROM fill (stub) and
              the image's low half; loading screen stub in bank 13, emulator-
              tested only

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
